WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.406
Three workbench series, three very different jobs.

00:00:05.686 --> 00:00:09.357
Pick the right one, and your bench quietly does its work for years.

00:00:09.637 --> 00:00:12.268
Pick the wrong one, and you will feel it every day.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:15.537
Teams often buy one bench type for everything.

00:00:15.817 --> 00:00:20.935
Then a grinder shakes a light bench, or a lab pays for heavy-duty steel it never needed.

00:00:21.535 --> 00:00:29.604
Base is the multipurpose bench for general assembly, packing and training, rated at 454 kilos UDL.

00:00:29.884 --> 00:00:36.345
Scitec is built for electronics, labs and testing, and can stand on legs, base cabinets, or both.

00:00:36.625 --> 00:00:42.287
Pro is the industrial-grade series for vices, grinders, test machines and rough work.

00:00:42.887 --> 00:00:45.208
Each series takes a range of worktops,

00:00:45.208 --> 00:00:49.055
so the frame matches the load and the surface matches the task.

00:00:49.335 --> 00:00:53.517
And because Link accessories fit all three series, you can add shelves,

00:00:53.517 --> 00:00:56.403
power and lighting to whichever bench you choose.

00:00:57.003 --> 00:00:59.203
Simple rule: general work, Base.

00:00:59.483 --> 00:01:01.029
Technical work, Scitec.

00:01:01.309 --> 00:01:02.807
Heavy or rough work, Pro.

00:01:03.087 --> 00:01:04.400
Which one fits your line?

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:09.698
Comment below, and next, learn why some benches stand on cabinets instead of legs.

00:01:10.298 --> 00:01:14.543
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

